# Secrets — API keys live in the shell environment, never in the repo
.env
.env.*
# .env.example holds placeholders only and is safe to commit.
!.env.example
*.key

# Data. Two of these are COMMITTED, and the distinction is reproducibility.
#
# interpretations.jsonl (3.6 MB) is irreplaceable. It is 2,552 paid teacher
# calls at temperature 0.3-0.5, so re-running produces DIFFERENT TEXT and a
# different corpus. Without it in the repo nobody — including us after a disk
# failure — could verify or rebuild a single reported number.
#
# raw_poems.jsonl (13 MB) is re-fetchable, but committing it pins exactly what
# PoetryDB served on the day. The API is a live service with no versioning; a
# poem edited upstream would silently change the corpus under a future reader.
#
# Backups and scratch copies are NOT committed: they are snapshots of moments
# nothing references, and shipping several near-identical corpora invites the
# wrong one being read.
data/*
!data/sample/
!data/sample/**
!data/interpretations.jsonl
!data/raw_poems.jsonl
!data/folds.json
# The outer split: test ids, pool ids, tuning folds. Committed for the same
# reason as folds.json — it is computed once locally and shipped to the GPU
# side as data, and recomputing it there with a different seed would break the
# held-out guarantee without raising anything.
!data/holdout.json
# training_pairs.jsonl (6.2 MB) is derived from the two above, so it looks
# redundant — but it is the file Kaggle trains on, and CLAUDE.md forbids
# rebuilding it there: the funnel is a pure function of the raw files AND the
# thresholds, so a threshold changed after the folds were written would have the
# GPU side training on a different set of poems than the assignment describes,
# with nothing raising.
#
# It must also travel WITH folds.json, which is already committed. Shipping one
# without the other is precisely the "stale half" the single-save rule exists to
# prevent, and it is what left Kaggle with an assignment and no corpus.
!data/training_pairs.jsonl
data/*.bak
data/*.pre-retry.*

# results/ IS committed — runs.csv, figures and the LoRA adapters are part of
# the deliverable. Only transient checkpoints are excluded.
results/checkpoints/
*.ckpt

# Smoke artifacts are gpt2 output from five-step runs. They exist to prove the
# code executes, not to be read as results, and a reader finding runs.csv next
# to smoke_runs.csv has to work out which is which. Everything SMOKE writes
# carries this prefix, so one rule covers all of it.
results/smoke_*
results/adapters/smoke_*
results/histories/smoke.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.virtual_documents/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code — local tooling, not part of the deliverable
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Transfer archives — their contents are already extracted alongside them.
results/session_output*.zip
results/to_download/
